  "gaps": [
    "Credit unit is printed only as 'credits'; the capture does not explicitly state semester credits for this program (semester assumed; the only 'semester units' wording appears in the California CPA note for the Accounting program).",
    "GEN 101 is labeled 'Entry Point Course ... (Elective)'. The 10 listed Foundations courses (30 credits) plus the 6 core credits that also satisfy Foundations total 36, not the stated 33, which suggests GEN 101 counts toward the 13 elective credits rather than toward Foundations. The capture does not state this explicitly. Listing GEN 101 separately alongside the 13-credit elective block gives a ledger sum of 70 against the 67 printed total, so the open-elective remainder may be 10 credits. This needs confirmation.",
    "Six core credits (BUS 114 for Interdisciplinary Critical Thinking and BUS 340 for Interdisciplinary Oral Communication) also satisfy Global Campus Foundations requirements. They are listed once under core.",
    "Residency: 'At least 18 credits earned toward the Associate of Arts degree must be completed at the University of Arizona Global Campus.' The capture does not tie this to specific courses, so no course is marked institutionalOnly.",
    "Minimum cumulative GPA of 2.00 is required; course-level minimum grades are not stated.",
    "'Additional prerequisite courses may be required' — the capture does not state the prerequisites for the core courses (e.g., the 300-level BUS 303, BUS 330, BUS 340).",
    "The capture also contains the beginning of the Bachelor of Arts in Accounting (120 credits). That section is truncated after BUS 308 and has not been extracted here; its remaining major courses, Foundations courses, and elective details are not in the capture."
  ],
